// Prisma Schema for FreshLoop AI - Yield Management & Recipe Rescue
// Phase 1: Database Schema bridge (additive — preserves existing tables/columns)
//
// Bridges current production models to architecture needs from CLAUDE.md /
// Inventory · Recipe · Price agents:
//   1. Item Aging        — receivedDate + indexes for "in inventory > N days"
//   2. Revenue Lost      — originalUnitPrice vs discountedPrice (+ WasteEvent)
//   3. Recipe Logic      — RecipeIngredient rows + numeric portion yield
//   4. Agent support     — PosSale, WasteEvent, DailyWasteMetric, PriceAction,
//                          BundleOffer, SmartAlert, VoiceLogItem
// =============================================================================
// FreshLoop AI — Phase 1 Database Schema (Master Development Plan)
// =============================================================================
// RULE 1 (The Ledger): NEVER treat static "Current Stock" as source of truth.
//   Product on-hand quantity MUST be derived via SUM(InventoryTransaction.qtyChange)
//   filtered by product (+ optional location). InventoryItem.quantity is LEGACY only.
// RULE 2 (Location Tracking): Every InventoryTransaction MUST set fromLocation
//   and toLocation (e.g. Retail_Floor, Kitchen_Prep, Waste_Bin, Receiving, POS).
//
// This file implements Master Plan Phase 1 models AND preserves LEGACY/BRIDGE
// tables the live Next.js app still references (VendorInvoice, InvoiceLineItem,
// InventoryItem, VoiceLog, RecipeFusion + existing enums).
// =============================================================================
// ============================================================================
// FreshLoop AI — Enterprise Relational Database Schema (Phase 1)
// Architecture Rules:
//   1. Immutable Ledger: NO static "Current Stock" columns on Product.
//      Stock is strictly computed by summing Qty_Change in InventoryTransaction.
//   2. Mandatory Locations: Every InventoryTransaction records From_Location
//      and To_Location (e.g. Retail_Floor, Kitchen_Prep, Waste_Bin).
// ============================================================================

generator client {
  provider = "prisma-client-js"
}

datasource db {
  provider  = "postgresql"
  url       = env("DATABASE_URL")
  directUrl = env("DIRECT_URL")
}

